        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "### Measurement contract\n- **DB offload ratio** is the share of completed cache outcomes that did not execute this request's DB loader. It includes Redis hits and JVM single-flight coalescing.\n- **Redis hit ratio** counts values served from Redis (`hit`, `hit_after_wait`, `negative_hit`) and excludes coalesced DB results.\n- Request outcomes do not include failed DB loads; inspect **DB load outcome RPS** for `error`. Latency quantiles use successful `found` loads and `acquired` locks.\n- `outbox` eviction success means the durable replay attempt completed. Because every change is replayed and retries count as attempts, it is not a count of proven stale-cache repairs. Use **All instances** when comparing fast and durable paths because Kafka may consume the replay on another application instance.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
